WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0143: the offscreen window follows BG3's picture size (on top of 0001-0142).

The window kept the size WOW_WIN gave it at start (BG3's settings file then). A resolution or aspect ratio changed in
BG3's options while playing left WoW rendering at the old size, and the render plugin stretched it over BG3's picture
(horizontal lines, a wrong aspect: seen on an Nvidia PC going from 1280x720 to 2560x1080). The render plugin writes
BG3's swapchain size to $WOW_BG3_LINK_DIR/bg3size.txt ("W H") whenever BG3 makes one; follow_bg3_size reads it
(at most every 250 ms, when its time changes) and sets the window's physical size; retarget makes the cameras' image
of that size as for any resize.

